y at large every four years.\nThe County Treasurer is a position that is elected at large. The Treasurer's main responsibility is for the safe and prudent investments of county monies. The Treasurer is also responsible of receipting, balancing, reconciling and ensuring that monies are correctly accounted for in separate funds required by Missouri Law. Currently Mississippi County has 40 plus separate funds to maintain.\nRELATED LINKS:\nMISSOURI TREASURER'S WEB SITE\nwww.treasurer.mo.gov\nMISSOURI ASSOCIATION OF COUNTIES\nwww.mocounties.com\nCONTACT INFORMATION:\nMAIL\n200 N Main St., 1st Floor\nCHARLESTON, MO 63834\nPHONE#\n(573)-683-2146 EXT. 2235\nDirect Line (573) 683-2985\nFAX#\n(573)-683-6071\nEMAIL:\npmoore@misscomo.net\nShare this page\nShare this page\n×\nCopy and paste this code into your website.\n<a href=\"http://misscomo.net/services/treasurer.php\">Your Link Name</a>\nShare this page on your favorite Social network\nFacebook\nTwitter\nReddit\nClose\n(573) 683-2146\nMonday - Friday 8:00 a.m. - 4:30 p.m.\nPowered by revize . , the Government Website Experts | Login\nClose\nRead More\nOriginal text\nRate this translation\nYour feedback will be used to help improve Google Translate",
